 @Demon09-_-  I wish I could but it's been almost 2 months since 3070 Ti launch when I bought mine, don't think I could return it and get a 3080 at this point since I just sold my 1070 for $300 USD to some local guy before GPU prices tank once again.

In order to get my 1070 back in 2017 I had to initially buy a 1050 Ti from Best Buy for $150, then return it a week later when I had more money, get my money back and throw that towards a 1060, then do the same thing a week later to get my 1070.  It was really interesting to see the incremental increase in performance playing with each different card.

Tbh the 1050 Ti for only $150 back in 2017 was a really really good deal, the 1060 was like $275 or 300 or something and wasn't that big of an increase, so I was definitely happy I spent a little more and got the 1070 for $375 (was MSRP $445 but got a nice price matching steal showing the Best Buy clerk the wrong model number but same general gpu).

